# TODO - Journaled quiz publication

## Objective

Connect canonical create/edit execution with fresh remote read-back, strict
media admission, conflict detection, pacing, and recovery.

## Acceptance

**IT WORKS** when an authorized teacher request through the canonical
CLI/MCP flow can create and edit an admitted Blooket quiz (questions, types,
timing, and supported media), then re-read the remote quiz and confirm the
intended result. The workflow must retain recoverable progress and avoid
creating duplicate sets or questions after uncertain outcomes.

Demonstrate at least one real end-to-end publication through this product, plus
targeted tests for interruption, conflicting edits, and media admission.
Reject unsupported or unsafe operations visibly; do not label a saved local
draft or a synthetic transport fixture as published. Extra polish, theoretical
platform cases, and expanding test coverage belong to the final ongoing task.

## Implementation notes

Use the existing validated IR, write-plan lowering, persisted attempt journals,
checkpoints, receipts, locks, read-back, and reconciliation. Do not add a second
unprotected publication loop. Extend remote reads to validated question/media
state and detect concurrent online edits before changing a quiz.

Expose canonical CLI commands and MCP tools for list/read/create/edit, question
type, per-question seconds, stable-ID media selection, progress, and recovery.
Fresh verified Blooket state and the teacher's online request drive changes;
local draft JSON remains private automatic recovery state.

Resolve prepared media by stable ID and validate current recipe revision, actual
file format, and actual bytes before every upload. Upload only a prepared
rendition strictly below 2,500,000 bytes, never a larger original or stale file.
Reuse the same guard in UI, CLI, HTTP, browser, and MCP execution.

Run a small publication through this application's actual MCP/CLI
runtime, read it back after refresh, and test interruption, recovery, ambiguity,
account limits, and unsupported types. The existing private UI test is useful
evidence but does not replace this missing end-to-end flow.

## Evidence

Persisted execution now closes the pacing conflict window before mutation. It
captures the verification baseline, waits for its shared mutation lease, then
re-observes the session without authenticating and revalidates remote state.
Changed digests return an explicit remote-precondition conflict; expired,
rate-limited, and human-challenge states stop before task-budget reservation or
the attempt journal.

Write-time media admission now enumerates stable media IDs in canonical
operation order and deduplicates repeated references. Every referenced item must
resolve to a current prepared revision, admitted GIF/JPEG/PNG bytes, and a
positive revision, with the canonical exclusive 2,500,000-byte ceiling applied
to the actual byte snapshot. Missing, stale, malformed, oversized, or
unavailable media stops before budget reservation and journaling.

The browser-service composition adapts the current teacher library into this
media port using the current configured canvas and the existing strict prepared
read. That read already validates current recipe revision, rendition identity,
actual byte count, decoded dimensions, and file format. The exact admitted
Uint8Array snapshot is carried through the write execution port into the browser
surface so publication does not re-resolve a different file after the journal
opens.

A concrete text-only Create Set browser surface now exists behind the local
browser bridge. It navigates the dedicated Blooket tab to the observed create
form and fills only the verified title/description/privacy controls. It
revalidates the
exact prepared state before one submit click, and confirms success only after
the provider reaches an exact /edit?id=... redirect.

Challenge, organization, rate-limit, expired-session, signed-out, timeout,
malformed DOM, and malformed bridge outcomes remain explicit stops or failures
rather than success.

The browser-service runtime composes that bridge surface through the existing
canonical BlooketWriteExecutionPort and prepared-media port. The bridge
command is internal. Canonical publication commands now enter through the
persisted executor, preserving task budgets, pacing, journals, and
reconciliation.

Synthetic persisted-runtime coverage now exercises the complete guarded
Create Set path. It reobserves the browser session, durably reserves the task
budget, opens the attempt journal, crosses the local bridge once, converts the
observed remote ID into a receipt, advances the checkpoint, and clears the
journal. A challenge before mutation creates neither budget nor journal; a
challenge during the bridge mutation consumes one budget start and preserves
the attempting journal for reconciliation without replay.

### Canonical text-only publication foundation

On 2026-10-08, logical draft-ID commands were connected through the ordinary
CLI and admitted MCP tools to the local service. The first step requires the
exact saved revision, admits account capabilities, and durably freezes the
project/capability snapshot before journaled execution. Each call performs at
most one set/question write; caller paths and retry overrides are rejected.

Progress remains separate from publication proof. Final verification requires
completed checkpoints, no uncertain attempt, exact remote metadata/question
state, and two matching fresh observations. Unsupported media is refused before
snapshot creation or provider inspection; editing existing quizzes is not
claimed by this creation-only command family.

Targeted portable tests cover revision conflicts, concurrent duplicate steps,
uncertain outcomes/reconciliation, cancellation after journal persistence,
unsupported media, immutable bounded storage, and changed remote observations.
An integration fixture crosses real MCP, CLI subprocess, HTTP, persistence, and
browser-bridge boundaries with a simulated provider. Live canonical publication
remains pending and this record stays active.

Strict TypeScript, roadmap integrity, and all 1042 portable tests passed at this
checkpoint with Node test concurrency limited to four. The unbounded full run
exhausted process/browser timing windows; its failed result is not acceptance.
Jig validation returned zero repository diagnostics, while its existing graph
rule evaluation limitation remains explicit in the development handoff.

## Blockers

Text-only Add Question browser mechanics now submit once and require exact
post-submit read-back. Media upload, existing-quiz editing, and live canonical
publication acceptance remain pending. The connected legacy extension must be
replaced before the current bounded read contracts can verify a real result.

Safari, macOS, and ChatGPT-specific hardening belongs only to task blooket-15
and does not block this functional record.
